{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvaaB74R8KufMnurw85b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**I'd treat the non-buyer survey as a minor input, not the basis for the decision.**\n\n**Why the survey is weak**\n- Stated willingness to pay is unreliable. Non-buyers will usually say \"cheaper would work\", and that costs them nothing to say.\n- The miss is roughly 10x (0.3% vs 3%). If 20,000 is the treated group, that's about 60 buyers. A price cut would have to do far more than shave the gap.\n- The 40% refund rate points to a value or expectation problem, not only a price problem. Even people who wanted it at £15 regretted it. A cheaper price could raise sign-ups and refunds together. Non-buyers can't tell you why buyers refunded.\n- Net retained take-up is about 0.18% (about 36 customers), which is the number to judge against the target.\n\n**What I'd do instead**\n1. **Ask the refunders and buyers why.** It's a small group, so interviews are cheap and more informative than a broad survey.\n2. **Look at the funnel.** Check how many people saw the offer, clicked, and reached checkout. If almost nobody clicked, the problem is positioning or demand. If many abandoned at checkout, price becomes more plausible.\n3. **Check how the 3% target was set.** If it was aspirational, the product may still be viable at a lower take-up and the target may be the problem.\n4. **If price is still the open question, test it with real behaviour.** Randomise two or three price points (for example £5, £9 and £15) and measure net take-up after refunds, not gross sign-ups.\n5. **Judge it on outcomes, not just sales.** Compare buyers against the control group on support contacts, satisfaction and churn. That shows whether the add-on is worth having at any price.\n\n**Decision:** don't launch, and don't cut the price on survey evidence alone. Do steps 1–3 first, since they're quick and cheap, then decide whether a price test is worth running."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3601,"cache_read_input_tokens":4609,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3601},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66b5cce6-8b1e-44ac-aefb-1ab5d81043d6","uuid":"488e34dd-7074-4f99-95de-3c0dd9fb36b0","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:07:20.728Z","request_id":"req_011CfvaaApgcwva9sqvqCU4M"}
